{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLArpeggiate\/placement"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlarpeggiate\/placement"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"placement","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLAboveBelow","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAboveBelow","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL13MXLAboveBelowO"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","text":"Discussion","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Maps to the MusicXML ","type":"text"},{"code":"placement","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" attribute.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The placement attribute indicates whether something is above or below another element, such as a note or a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"notation."}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLArpeggiate"]]},"metadata":{"fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"placement","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLAboveBelow","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL13MXLAboveBelowO"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"roleHeading":"Instance Property","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL13MXLArpeggiateV9placementAA13MXLAboveBelowOSgvp","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"title":"placement","symbolKind":"property","role":"symbol"},"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLArpeggiate":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlarpeggiate","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLArpeggiate","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The arpeggiate type indicates that this note is part of an arpeggiated chord. The number attribute can be used"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to distinguish between two simultaneous chords arpeggiated separately (different numbers) or together (same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"number). The direction attribute is used if there is an arrow on the arpeggio sign. By default, arpeggios go"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from the lowest to highest note. The length of the sign can be determined from the position attributes for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"arpeggiate elements used with the top and bottom notes of the arpeggiated chord. If the unbroken attribute is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"set to yes, it indicates that the arpeggio continues onto another staff within the part. This serves as a hint"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to applications and is not required for cross-staff arpeggios."}],"title":"MXLArpeggiate","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLArpeggiate","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLArpeggiate","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLAboveBelow":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlabovebelow","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAboveBelow","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLAboveBelow"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The above-below type is used to indicate whether one element appears above or below another element.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLAboveBelow"}],"title":"MXLAboveBelow"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLArpeggiate/placement":{"abstract":[{"text":"The placement attribute indicates whether something is above or below another element, such as a note or a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"notation.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlarpeggiate\/placement","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"placement"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLAboveBelow","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL13MXLAboveBelowO"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLArpeggiate\/placement","role":"symbol","title":"placement","type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","title":"IvorMXL","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","kind":"symbol"}}}